hardcase_div.py: closest-approach divisions, constructed, verified, and measured against the campaign's sampler

== H1. construction: one modular inverse a divisor, |N| = 1 verified in exact integers
   fp32   mid +1: built for 1170 of 3000 odd divisors (39.0%), |N| = 1 verified on all of them (0 wrong)
   fp32   mid -1: built for 1145 of 3000 odd divisors (38.2%), |N| = 1 verified on all of them (0 wrong)
   fp32   rep +1: built for 1119 of 3000 odd divisors (37.3%), |N| = 1 verified on all of them (0 wrong)
   fp32   rep -1: built for 1156 of 3000 odd divisors (38.5%), |N| = 1 verified on all of them (0 wrong)
CHECK fp32: every constructed dividend has |N| = 1 exactly and lies in [my, 2^p)                       ok 
CHECK fp32: the construction succeeds for 30 to 45% of odd divisors per sign (about 2 ln 2 - 1 = 38.6%) ok (38.6%)
   fp64   mid +1: built for 1215 of 3000 odd divisors (40.5%), |N| = 1 verified on all of them (0 wrong)
   fp64   mid -1: built for 1159 of 3000 odd divisors (38.6%), |N| = 1 verified on all of them (0 wrong)
   fp64   rep +1: built for 1137 of 3000 odd divisors (37.9%), |N| = 1 verified on all of them (0 wrong)
   fp64   rep -1: built for 1167 of 3000 odd divisors (38.9%), |N| = 1 verified on all of them (0 wrong)
CHECK fp64: every constructed dividend has |N| = 1 exactly and lies in [my, 2^p)                       ok 
CHECK fp64: the construction succeeds for 30 to 45% of odd divisors per sign (about 2 ln 2 - 1 = 38.6%) ok (39.6%)
   fp128  mid +1: built for 1170 of 3000 odd divisors (39.0%), |N| = 1 verified on all of them (0 wrong)
   fp128  mid -1: built for 1125 of 3000 odd divisors (37.5%), |N| = 1 verified on all of them (0 wrong)
   fp128  rep +1: built for 1177 of 3000 odd divisors (39.2%), |N| = 1 verified on all of them (0 wrong)
   fp128  rep -1: built for 1160 of 3000 odd divisors (38.7%), |N| = 1 verified on all of them (0 wrong)
CHECK fp128: every constructed dividend has |N| = 1 exactly and lies in [my, 2^p)                      ok 
CHECK fp128: the construction succeeds for 30 to 45% of odd divisors per sign (about 2 ln 2 - 1 = 38.6%) ok (38.2%)

== H2. the golden model's division on the closest-approach cases against an independent exact arbiter
CHECK fp32: golden div = exact arbiter on 300 constructed pairs x 5 attributes (bits and flags)        ok (1500 cases, 0 differ)
CHECK fp64: golden div = exact arbiter on 300 constructed pairs x 5 attributes (bits and flags)        ok (1500 cases, 0 differ)
CHECK fp128: golden div = exact arbiter on 120 constructed pairs x 5 attributes (bits and flags)       ok (600 cases, 0 differ)
CHECK CONTROL: the arbiter's RNE answer differs from the model's RTZ answer on the near-midpoint cases (the comparison can see) ok (200 of 200)

== H3. how close does the campaign's sampler come, and how many closest-approach cases would a weekend meet?
   rho = |N| / my in [0, 1] is the distance to the nearest midpoint in units of half an ulp; |N| = 1 is the closest approach a divisor can allow
   (only an ODD divisor allows it: N is a multiple of the divisor's power of two). Two boundary types, a midpoint and a representable number,
   each with its own |N| = 1 set; the per-draw probability of ONE type is counted below, exactly where a count is possible.

   the count of |N| = 1 pairs, one boundary type, p-bit significand pairs (dividend doubled when mx < my, as the sampler does):
   p    type          pairs    brute force    sum of 1/my  closed form count/closed
   8    mid           16384             87             87         88.7        0.981
   8    rep           16384             84             84         88.7        0.947
   10   mid          262144            359            359        354.9        1.012
   10   rep          262144            336            336        354.9        0.947
   11   mid         1048576            703            703        709.8        0.990
   11   rep         1048576            702            702        709.8        0.989
CHECK the sum over odd divisors of the solutions of X 2^k = +-1 equals the brute-force count of |N| = 1 pairs, p = 8, 10, 11, both types ok 
CHECK the closed form ln 2 / 2^(p-1) a draw is within 5% of the exhaustive count at p = 11, both types ok (0.990, 0.989)
CHECK CONTROL: the first draft's rate, 2 / (1.5 2^(p-1)) a draw, is NOT within 5% of the exhaustive count (it is out by a factor of about 1.9) ok (1.94 times the exhaustive rate at p = 11)

   exactly at p = 24 (every odd divisor): midpoint 5815346 of 2^46 pairs (8.2641e-08 a draw), representable 5812730 (8.2604e-08); ln 2 / 2^23 = 8.2630e-08
CHECK at p = 24 the exact count is within 0.1% of ln 2 / 2^23 a draw, both types                       ok (1.00014, 0.99969)

   p = 24  200000 sampled odd divisors: solutions a divisor, midpoint 1.3873, representable 1.3858 (2 ln 2 = 1.3863): 8.269e-08 and 8.260e-08 a draw
CHECK fp32: the sampled mean number of solutions a divisor is within 2% of 2 ln 2, both types          ok 
CHECK fp32: the per-draw probability used below is ln 2 / 2^(p-1) within 2%, both types (a factor 2 slip is caught here) ok (1.001, 1.000)
   p = 53  200000 sampled odd divisors: solutions a divisor, midpoint 1.3858, representable 1.3848 (2 ln 2 = 1.3863): 1.539e-16 and 1.537e-16 a draw
CHECK fp64: the sampled mean number of solutions a divisor is within 2% of 2 ln 2, both types          ok 
CHECK fp64: the per-draw probability used below is ln 2 / 2^(p-1) within 2%, both types (a factor 2 slip is caught here) ok (1.000, 0.999)
   p = 113 200000 sampled odd divisors: solutions a divisor, midpoint 1.3845, representable 1.3855 (2 ln 2 = 1.3863): 1.333e-34 and 1.334e-34 a draw
CHECK fp128: the sampled mean number of solutions a divisor is within 2% of 2 ln 2, both types         ok 
CHECK fp128: the per-draw probability used below is ln 2 / 2^(p-1) within 2%, both types (a factor 2 slip is caught here) ok (0.999, 0.999)

   how close the campaign's own sampler comes (its port, held to the real tool in seed_audit.py): the least rho over its draws,
   against the expected number of closest-approach hits in a stress-run-sized item (14498660352 draws; an UPPER bound: a draw whose quotient is
   subnormal or overflows has another boundary, and a banded operand is not a uniform significand)
   format   draws here   least rho here     least possible rho         hits, one type       hits, both types
   fp32         358161        2.307e-06              5.960e-08                1.2e+03                2.4e+03
CHECK fp32: the least rho over 358161 draws is within a factor 10 of 1 / draws, as uniform draws predict ok (2.31e-06 against 2.79e-06)
   fp64         362061        8.888e-07              1.110e-16               2.23e-06               4.46e-06
CHECK fp64: the least rho over 362061 draws is within a factor 10 of 1 / draws, as uniform draws predict ok (8.89e-07 against 2.76e-06)
CHECK fp32: the stress run's draws (1.45e10 a division item) expect over 1,000 closest-approach hits of the midpoint type alone ok (1199, and 2396 of both types)
CHECK fp64: the same draws expect fewer than 10^-5 of either type (the class is invisible to sampling) ok (2.23e-06, and 4.46e-06 of both types)

== H4. the repository's own failure family: a = 1, b = 1 - ulp (python/tests/test_sequences.py)
   fp32   |N| = 1, rho = |N| / my = 5.960e-08 = 1 / my: a closest-approach case (the quotient is 1/(my 2^p), about 2^-48, from a midpoint: 2^-25 of an ulp)
CHECK fp32: (1, 1 - ulp) has |N| <= 2, i.e. is within a factor 2 of the closest possible approach to a midpoint ok (|N| = 1)
   fp64   |N| = 1, rho = |N| / my = 1.110e-16 = 1 / my: a closest-approach case (the quotient is 1/(my 2^p), about 2^-106, from a midpoint: 2^-54 of an ulp)
CHECK fp64: (1, 1 - ulp) has |N| <= 2, i.e. is within a factor 2 of the closest possible approach to a midpoint ok (|N| = 1)

== H5. a PLANTED defect only the constructed set finds: the quotient computed to g extra bits, rounded ties-to-even on those bits alone
   the flawed division (g = 40 extra bits) at fp64: 0 failures in 272007 sampler draws; 606 failures in 2374 constructed closest-approach pairs
   expected failures in a stress-run-sized item (1.45e10 draws): about 6.59e-03
CHECK the sampler finds NO failure of the flawed division in 300,000 draws                             ok (0)
CHECK the constructed closest-approach set finds the flawed division FAILING on about a quarter of its midpoint pairs at least ok (606 of 2374)
CHECK a stress-run-sized item would expect under 0.01 failures: the defect would pass the weekend      ok (6.59e-03)
CHECK CONTROL: with g = 80 extra bits the same method is correct on every constructed pair (the set does not just fail everything) ok (0 failures)

== H6. square root: where is the closest approach to a midpoint? (fp32, every midpoint of the binade pair [1, 4))
   least d over the 8388608 midpoints: 1, reached by 2 midpoint(s); the next values of d: [1, 7, 9, 15, 17, 23]
CHECK fp32: the least d is 1 (a closest approach of 2^-48 to the midpoint M^2: the minimum an odd square allows) ok (d = 1)
CHECK fp32: sqrt(1 + ulp), the repository's failure family under RMM (python/tests/test_sequences.py), has d = 1 ok (d = 1)
   the 2 midpoint(s) with d = 1 of the 8388608; sampling reaches such an input with probability about 2 / 2^24 a draw
CHECK fp32: golden sqrt = an exact integer arbiter on every closest-approach input (d = 1), all 5 attributes ok (10 cases, 0 differ)

hardcase_div: every CHECK held
